<topic id="alerts">
  <title>Alerts</title>
  <shortdesc>Provide contextual feedback messages for typical user actions with the handful of available and flexible
    alert messages.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Alerts</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlatt>otherprops</xmlatt></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>note</xmlelement></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlelement>section</xmlelement></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section id="default-alert">
      <title>Default alert</title>
      <p>Alerts are available for any length of text, as well as an optional close button. Alerts are designed to be
        used with theme colors, but have neutral fallback colors for when no theme color is applied.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Default alert</title>
      <image href="src/alerts/basic.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/basic.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/basic.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section id="variants">
      <title>Variants</title>
      <p>Use any of the eight variant theme classes for color mode adaptive, contextual styling (e.g., set
          <xmlatt>theme</xmlatt> to <codeph>success</codeph>).</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Variants</title>
      <image href="src/alerts/variants.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/variants.xml"/></codeblock>

    <section id="additional-content">
      <title>Additional content</title>
      <p>Alerts can also contain additional HTML elements like headings, paragraphs, icons and links.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Additional content</title>
      <image href="src/alerts/additional-content.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/additional-content.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/additional-content.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <section id="with-icons">
      <title>With icons</title>
      <p>Similarly, you can use flexbox utilities and Bootstrap Icons to create alerts with icons. Depending on your
        icons and content, you may want to add more utilities or custom styles.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>With icons</title>
      <image href="src/alerts/with-icons.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/with-icons.xml"/></codeblock>

    <section id="notes">
      <title>Notes</title>
      <p>DITA <xmlelement>note</xmlelement> elements are displayed as alerts according to the <xmlatt>type</xmlatt>
        attribute. With the exception <xmlatt>type="othertype"</xmlatt>, an icon is added if <xmlatt
        >type</xmlatt> is present.</p>
    </section>
<fig>
      <title>Notes</title>
      <image href="src/alerts/notes.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/notes.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/notes.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
    <p>The default colors can be overridden by using a <xmlatt>theme</xmlatt> attribute or an <xmlatt
      >outputclass</xmlatt>.</p>
<fig>
      <title>Note colors</title>
      <image href="src/alerts/note-colors.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/note-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/note-colors.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>

    <p>Use an additional <xmlatt>icon</xmlatt> attribute or <xmlatt>otherprops</xmlatt> to alter the default icon.</p>
<fig>
      <title>Note icons</title>
      <image href="src/alerts/note-icons.png" scalefit="yes"/>
    </fig>
    <tabbed-dialog style="pills" margin="t3">
      <section>
        <title>Specialization</title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/specialization/alerts/note-icons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
      <section>
        <title><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></title>
        <codeblock><coderef href="code/html/alerts/note-icons.xml"/></codeblock>
      </section>
    </tabbed-dialog>
  </body>
</topic>
